abstract: >-
  TLS13-H3-IDS-2026 is a labelled network intrusion-detection dataset captured
  on a physically air-gapped four-host testbed in which web services are
  delivered exclusively over TLS 1.3 and HTTP/3. Benign traffic is produced by
  a suite of non-browser Python HTTP clients; the attacks comprise network
  reconnaissance, application-layer credential brute-forcing, and HTTP/3
  flooding denial-of-service directed at the encrypted services. Both TCP
  (TLS 1.3) and QUIC/HTTP-3 carry benign and malicious traffic, so attacks
  cannot be separated by transport alone. Ground truth is effect-verified,
  leakage is precluded by construction and by an enforced temporal partition,
  and the entire generation pipeline is released with per-run cryptographic
  provenance. The corpus comprises 153,193 labelled flows across seven attack
  runs.

